  {
    "n": 1,
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "This section records some design and implementation details.",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 2,
    "tag": "h1",
    "text": "Architecture",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 3,
    "tag": "h2",
    "text": "SAX and DOM",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 4,
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "The basic relationships of SAX and DOM is shown in the following UML diagram.",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 5,
    "tag": "div",
    "text": "Architecture UML class diagram",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 6,
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "The core of the relationship is the {1} concept. From the SAX side, {2} parses a JSON from a stream and publish events to a {3}. {4} implements the {5} concept to handle the same set of events. From the DOM side, {6} implements the {7} concept to build a DOM according to the events. {8} supports a {9} function, which traverses the DOM to publish events.",
    "tokens": [
      "<span class=\"tt\"><a class=\"el\" href=\"/docs/rapidjson/v1-1-0/en/02-reference/047-classrapidjson_1_1_handler/\" title=\"Concept for receiving events from GenericReader upon parsing. The functions return true if no error o...\">Handler</a></span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">Reader</span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\"><a class=\"el\" href=\"/docs/rapidjson/v1-1-0/en/02-reference/047-classrapidjson_1_1_handler/\" title=\"Concept for receiving events from GenericReader upon parsing. The functions return true if no error o...\">Handler</a></span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">Writer</span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\"><a class=\"el\" href=\"/docs/rapidjson/v1-1-0/en/02-reference/047-classrapidjson_1_1_handler/\" title=\"Concept for receiving events from GenericReader upon parsing. The functions return true if no error o...\">Handler</a></span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">Document</span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\"><a class=\"el\" href=\"/docs/rapidjson/v1-1-0/en/02-reference/047-classrapidjson_1_1_handler/\" title=\"Concept for receiving events from GenericReader upon parsing. The functions return true if no error o...\">Handler</a></span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">Value</span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">Value::Accept(<a class=\"el\" href=\"/docs/rapidjson/v1-1-0/en/02-reference/047-classrapidjson_1_1_handler/\" title=\"Concept for receiving events from GenericReader upon parsing. The functions return true if no error o...\">Handler</a>&amp;)</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "n": 7,
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "With this design, SAX is not dependent on DOM. Even {1} and {2} have no dependencies between them. This provides flexibility to chain event publisher and handlers. Besides, {3} does not depends on SAX as well. So, in addition to stringify a DOM to JSON, user may also stringify it to a XML writer, or do anything else.",
    "tokens": [
      "<span class=\"tt\">Reader</span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">Writer</span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">Value</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "n": 8,
    "tag": "h2",
    "text": "Utility Classes",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 9,
    "tag": "p",
    "text": "Both SAX and DOM APIs depends on 3 additional concepts: {1}, {2} and {3}. Their inheritance hierarchy is shown as below.",
    "tokens": [
      "<span class=\"tt\"><a class=\"el\" href=\"/docs/rapidjson/v1-1-0/en/02-reference/005-classrapidjson_1_1_allocator/\" title=\"Concept for allocating, resizing and freeing memory block.\">Allocator</a></span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\"><a class=\"el\" href=\"/docs/rapidjson/v1-1-0/en/02-reference/022-classrapidjson_1_1_encoding/\" title=\"Concept for encoding of Unicode characters.\">Encoding</a></span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\"><a class=\"el\" href=\"/docs/rapidjson/v1-1-0/en/02-reference/056-classrapidjson_1_1_stream/\" title=\"Concept for reading and writing characters.\">Stream</a></span>"
    ]
  },
